---
import Head from "../components/Head.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import "../styles/site.css";
import "../styles/landing.css";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head><Head title="Contextful — local-first context for agents" description="A local-first context engine for agents and small teams. Versioned data, retrieval and memory through CLI, MCP and HTTP." /></head>
  <body class="landing">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <Header />
    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="kicker"><span></span> LOCAL-FIRST CONTEXT ENGINE</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">Your data.<br />Your agents.<br /><em>Your context.</em></h1>
          <p class="hero-description">Connect your sources. Keep versioned data on your own storage. Give agents retrieval and memory through CLI, MCP and HTTP.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="/docs/">Explore the docs <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            <a class="button" href="https://github.com/fractalboxdev/contextful">View on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-note">Open source · Apache-2.0 · Built in Rust</p>
        </div>
        <div class="system-panel" aria-label="Contextful data flow: sources, versioned storage, and agent interfaces">
          <div class="panel-heading"><span>CONTEXTFUL / SYSTEM</span><span>LOCAL NODE</span></div>
          <div class="system-row"><span class="step">01</span><div><h2>Connect sources</h2><p>Sandboxed component connectors</p></div><span class="node-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↳</span></div>
          <div class="system-row"><span class="step">02</span><div><h2>Keep the data</h2><p>Parquet · manifest · catalog</p></div><span class="node-symbol" aria-hidden="true">≡</span></div>
          <div class="system-row"><span class="step">03</span><div><h2>Serve context</h2><p>Query · retrieval · memory</p></div><span class="node-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
          <div class="interfaces"><span>CLI</span><span>MCP</span><span>HTTP</span></div>
          <p class="panel-footer">One node offline. Optional object-storage sync.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="principles" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
        <div class="section-heading"><p class="kicker">DESIGNED FOR OWNERSHIP</p><h2 id="principles-title">Context stays close<br />to the data.</h2></div>
        <div class="feature-grid">
          <article><span class="feature-number">01 / STORAGE</span><h3>Files you own.</h3><p>Versioned Parquet sits beside a JSON manifest and a rebuildable catalog. Object storage carries optional sync.</p><a href="/docs/guide/store/">Explore the store →</a></article>
          <article><span class="feature-number">02 / INTERFACES</span><h3>Context agents can use.</h3><p>A CLI, MCP endpoint and HTTP interface expose retrieval, memory and derived results from the same engine.</p><a href="/docs/guide/read/">Explore the read path →</a></article>
          <article><span class="feature-number">03 / CONTRACTS</span><h3>Behavior you can inspect.</h3><p>Addressable clauses define the system. Tests and formal proofs ground its computed implementation status.</p><a href="/docs/specs/">Read the specification →</a></article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="docs-callout"><div><p class="kicker">FROM OVERVIEW TO CONTRACT</p><h2>See how Contextful fits together.</h2><p>Start with the topology, follow a guide, or inspect the demonstrated behavior.</p></div><a class="button primary" href="/docs/">Open documentation ↗</a></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer"><a class="brand" href="/">Contextful</a><span>A local-first context engine.</span><nav aria-label="Footer"><a href="/docs/">Documentation</a><a href="/docs/specs/status/">Implementation status</a><a href="https://github.com/fractalboxdev/contextful/blob/main/LICENSE">Apache-2.0</a></nav></footer>
  </body>
</html>
